  "user_request_original": "Design a 10-layer planar multilayer dielectric film on Ge substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe (10 finite layers total). All layer thicknesses are optimizable variables with bounds 100-2000nm. Wavelength range 3000-11000nm sampled at 2001 points. Target: maximize transmittance in 8000-11000nm band, minimize transmittance in 3000-5000nm band. Use coherent TMM solver. Initialize thicknesses at 1000nm for all layers. Apply gradient_thickness and differential_evolution_thickness optimizers. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 8000-11000 nm, 3000-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band; Low transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count not exceeding 16.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design and optimize a 10-layer air-Ge planar stack with an alternating ZnS/ZnSe sequence for coherent normal-incidence operation over 3000–11000 nm. Maximize mean transmittance in the 8000–11000 nm band while minimizing mean transmittance in the 3000–5000 nm band. All ten coating layers have variable thicknesses constrained between 100 nm and 2000 nm, initialized at 1000 nm. Solve using a coherent transfer-matrix approach with gradient-based/L-BFGS optimization.",
